**What this PR does / why we need it**:

This PR is the first part of moving query history to be stored in database instead of browser's local storage. The design document is [here](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BdVtoXCxhH0Q6C-O_Z7jKi-u1m5pDoS9_HQKhYu_hEE/edit#) (we are later planning to introduce shared history, but that is out of scope for now).

To make PRs smaller and easier to review, I am splitting it into chunks. Here is the issue with steps: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/44327

This PR:

1. Creates API for patching the comment of query already stored in query history
2. After we update the comment, we return query history DTO

**Which issue(s) this PR fixes**:

Part of https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/44327

**Special notes for your reviewer**:

To test the functionality you can add this snippet to https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/public/app/features/explore/state/query.ts#L324 (you need to import { getBackendSrv } from '@grafana/runtime';

You also have to enable query history enabled = true flag in custom.ini.

```
  //To test adding and deleting of query history
  const dataSourceUid = queries[0]?.datasource?.uid;
  if (dataSourceUid) {
    const { result } = await getBackendSrv().post(`/api/query-history`, {
      dataSourceUid,
      queries,
    });

    //Right away we update comment in added history item
    getBackendSrv().patch(`/api/query-history/${result.uid}`, {
      comment: 'Test1',
    });
  }
  // End of test
```

If the feature is enabled, it should update the comment and return query history dto with new comment.  If not, it should show error.

